title the tail read, not generated
prompt Keaton said kg the linengrow tail -- 153 asserts across 56 small files.
think The temptation with a tail is a class table: match a shape, stamp a reason, move on. Grouped all 242 first to see whether that would be honest, and the largest family held 10. It would not have been.
think So the files were read. 118 more blocks in two batches, on top of the 57 from the densest eight -- 175 blocks across 64 files, and the room closes.
obs The waymark family was the one real class, 15 asserts across the SETU and LULU ladders, each comparing a fixture's own waymark to a literal. One reason serves all: a fixture carried into another ladder's suite names itself rather than passing as though it had proved something about that ladder.
obs pool_host_seam and its kin assert balances.issuer + balances.holder >= balances.issuer, which is an overflow check wearing an inequality. The reason says so: a sum smaller than one of its parts is the one sign the addition wrapped, and a ledger that wraps reports money nobody holds.
obs neth_apply_step reads as a crash-recovery contract once the reasons are written -- a root pending before a write, none pending after an apply, and the log the length it had before the crash. Three asserts that together say a partial write is rolled back rather than half-kept.
obs glow_sensors_grant and glow_network_grant both assert !self.granted, and the reason is the seam's whole purpose: a permission reading as granted before anyone asked is the fault it exists to prevent.
obs linengrow reads 409 of 409. Tree 96%, gap 614, from 13,235 eight rounds ago.
